SM(481,{"n":"Acts 21-22","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Acts 21-22.mp3","d":2120.8,"s":[[0.16,"Come and study holy scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.08,"Father Stephen is a former Protestant pastor and Bible teacher in the Reformed Church, but now an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.36,"Then Paul took the men, and the next day, having been purified with them, entered the temple to announce the expiration of the days of purification, at which time an offering should be made for each one of them."],[34.64,"So there is a period of time leading up to taking the Bible called the Days of Purification when they would fast, when they would pray."],[41.2,"It's talking about him being purified with them."],[43.04,"That means the ritual washings before you went into the temple."],[46.64,"Uh, so that you were clean."],[48.16,"Notice, St. Paul still does them."],[51.94,"He doesn't say, oh, this stuff's all old hat."],[54.84,"I've been baptized, so I don't I never need to, you know, do a ritual."],[58.92,"He doesn't say any of that"],[61.68,"Right? And he doesn't he never says, Well, I guess I'll go along with this, you know, to try to get back on the good side of the Jewish people."],[68.88,"He's fully committed to, hey, if they kill me, okay."],[73.36,"You know. He's doing this because he believes this is still a valid and important thing."],[83.04,"Now, when the seven days were almost ended, the Jews from Asia, remember, these are the ones who are following him around."],[90.72,"They're causing trouble."],[92.96,"Seeing him in the temple, stirred up the whole crowd and laid hands on him, crying out, Men of Israel, help."],[99.2,"This is the man who teaches all men everywhere against the people, the law and, this place."],[103.52,"this place. And furthermore, he also brought Greeks into the temple that has defiled holy"],[111.64,"So again, this stuff isn't true, but they say, hey, this is the guy who they've been bad mouthing around town."],[120.12,"Yeah. And he tells he teaches against the temple, he teaches against the law, he teaches against the Jewish people."],[126.21,"And now he brought a bunch of Greeks in here."],[129.49,"And that last one is especially bad."],[132.39,"Not because there's something horrible about Greeks."],[136.07,"But you have to remember at this point, because we saw uh Jesus and St."],[142.95,"John's Gospel come and celebrate it, they're celebrating the Faste of Hanukkah every year."],[148.21,"And what do they celebrate at the Feast of Hanukkah every year?"],[151.57,"They celebrate the restoration of the temple after the Greeks defiled it."],[155.65,"Uh-huh. Because the Greek king, Antiochus Epiphades IV, came and sacrificed a pig on the altar."],[163.73,"And that was referred to by them from the book of Daniel as the abomination of desolation."],[169.73,"So by saying he's brought Greeks into the temple."],[174.15,"This is this is the trigger."],[176.12,"This is they don't have anything to base that on."],[179.64,"I mean, they they can't produce the Greeks that they're gonna be."],[181.64,"Well, we're gonna see they have something vaguely that they're basing that on."],[188.12,"Or at least that would make it quasiiev-belable."],[190.56,"We'll put it that way."],[191.44,"Yeah. For a mob."],[193.3,"But so, but that's I mean, he they're they're appealing to this horrible historical atrocity, in everyone's mind, to get everyone."],[203.81,"We've talked before about how they didn't have the authority to execute anybody, but you can get a mob to tear somebody apart if you get them angry enough."],[210.43,"So that's what they're going for here."],[214.59,"For they had previously seen Trophimus the Ephesian with him in the city, whom they supposed that Paul had brought into the temple."],[222.53,"So that's that's what they're you know, basing it on."],[228.13,"Uh that supposed is even."],[231.13,"It's not like they honestly thought it."],[232.29,"It's more people had seen him around town with Greeks, and so if we say he brought them into the temple, they'll believe it"],[239.71,"Because he has this reputation for eating with Gentiles and going into their homes and all these things."],[249.23,"And all the city was disturbed, and the people ran together, seized Paul, and dragged him out of the temple, and immediately the doors were shut."],[258.67,"Okay. So uh the temple complex goes into lockdown."],[264.35,"We talked back in the beginning of the book of Acts how there was a group of guards, of Jewish guards, who are uh worked in the temple complex because uh the Jewish authorities had sort of cut a deal with the Romans because of course the Roman soldiers being Gentiles weren't allowed very far into the temple."],[285.75,"And so they said, okay, well, you can have your own Jewish guards in there, and we won't come in there as long as you keep peace and order in there."],[293.75,"But if something starts going down, we're gonna send our soldiers right in there, we don't care."],[300.79,"And so that's why the doors get, as soon as this mob goes, and the mob drags St."],[305.99,"Paul inside, as soon as they can, they shut all the doors."],[308.69,"To make it clear to the Roman authorities when they come to investigate this big disturbance that, oh, it's not going out of the temple."],[316.05,"We don't need to send anyone in there."],[317.94,"We don't need to."],[318.82,"to Because that is they're presuming that that's what's going happen."],[320.9,"Because that's what the Romans do when there's a mob"],[327.1,"They they send soldiers to go and kill everyone."],[329.74,"And they just keep killing people until the mob disperses."],[333.9,"Yeah. They didn't really care who it was."],[338.22,"They just wanted it to stop."],[339.34,"And that was their most effective means."],[345.1,"Now, as they were seeking to kill him, news came to the commander of the garrison that all Jerusalem was in an uproar."],[351.6,"So, word gets back to the Roman garrison that there's trouble breaking out."],[357.92,"He immediately took soldiers and centurions and ran down to them."],[362.0,"And when they saw the commander of the soldiers, they stopped beating Paul."],[367.48,"So Paul's being beaten by this angry mob, but as soon as the Romans show up, they're all like, oh, uh, what?"],[372.6,"Well, what? Nothing to see here."],[375.08,"Nothing? Nothing's going on."],[376.84,"Because they knew what would be next."],[381.8,"Then the commander came near and took him and commanded him to be bound with two chains, and he asked who he was and what he had done."],[389.96,"And some among the multitude cried one thing and some another."],[393.48,"So as you can see, they had a slightly different justice system than we at least try to have."],[398.3,"Where they show up and this man's being beaten, so they arrest him."],[403.26,"Well, he must be beating him for something."],[405.1,"This guy must be the one causing the trouble."],[407.47,"And uh then they don't ask him. what's going on"],[410.47,"Hey, why are these people beating you?"],[412.39,"They ask the crowd, uh, what did this guy do that you're all beating him."],[416.09,"Because they assumed it must be something."],[417.85,"Uh-huh. But they can't get their story straight."],[422.42,"Because none of them really know."],[424.66,"He hasn't actually really done anything."],[427.14,"So this group over here has heard one thing, this group's heard another thing, this group's heard another thing."],[432.98,"Yeah, so they're all just yelling various things."],[437.46,"So when he could not ascertain the truth because of the tumult, he commanded him to be taken into the barracks."],[445.14,"When he reached the stairs, he had to be carried by the soldiers because of the violence of the mob."],[449.86,"For the multitude of the people followed after, crying out away with him."],[453.38,"Okay So the mob keeps following them while they're dragging him back to the barracks."],[461.28,"Screaming and yelling stuff at him."],[463.54,"And he's so badly beaten that he can't even make it up the stairs into the barracks."],[468.66,"The uh Robot soldiers have to pick him up and carry him."],[473.94,"So they're taking him back there to interrogate him."],[477.94,"We know from earlier in the book that St."],[480.02,"Paul is a Roman citizen."],[482.1,"Very few Jews were."],[483.78,"So they probably would have presumed he wasn't."],[486.5,"So they're probably taking him there to beat and then kill him in order to find out what's going on and make an example out of him so there won't be any further rioting like this."],[501.34,"Then as Paul was about to be led into the barracks, he said to the commander, May I speak to you."],[508.7,"So they're about to go inside."],[511.18,"St. Paul thinks it wise to mention a couple things."],[515.12,"Before the beating, slash torture, slash punishment ensues."],[521.6,"He replied, Can you speak Greek?"],[524.0,"Are you not the Egyptian who some time ago stirred up a rebellion and led the 4,000 assassins out into the wilderness?"],[531.2,"Okay, so the commander thinks St."],[534.88,"Paul is somebody else."],[536.32,"So it's a good thing he spoke up."],[539.52,"There was this Egyptian who had started the. this Egyptian was not actually Egyptian ethnically"],[545.08,"This is another one of the we talked about how there was this whole sequence of phony messiahs all through the first century BC, first century AD, all the way up to Bar Kogva, beginning of the second century."],[559.4,"This was one of them."],[561.4,"This was one of them."],[562.52,"But it's not who yeah."],[565.08,"Yeah, it's just referred to."],[567.08,"Because at the time St."],[568.12,"Luke is writing this, everybody knew who that was."],[572.58,"So they think he's this person."],[574.94,"Remember, there's a huge Jewish community in Alexandria at this time."],[578.5,"So he's somebody from Egypt who came, presented himself as the the Messiah, went out into the desert, and had this big group of followers who are gonna be his army, and uh they hadn't caught him yet at this point."],[594.51,"Um the Romans eventually caught up with those folks and killed, crucified them all."],[600.43,"Um that was after uh Lord Jesus crucified."],[606.27,"Yeah. So people came and said they claimed that they are the Messiah."],[610.43,"Yeah. Wow. Because of course we've got this big group of Jews who don't believe still that Jesus was the Messiah."],[617.33,"And Jesus prophesied that."],[619.89,"In in both St."],[621.17,"Matthew's Gospel and St."],[622.21,"Luke's Gospel. He said that people will come, you know, and so he's over here, he is over there, and don't believe them."],[630.81,"He says, when I return, everybody will know."],[635.15,"He says it's like when lightning flashes in the sky from the east to the west."],[638.51,"You you'll know when it's me."],[640.27,"Don't listen to any of these other people."],[644.19,"But Paul said, I am a Jew from Tarsus in Cilicia, a citizen of no mean city, and I implore you, permit me to speak to the people."],[653.23,"Okay. So he says, No, that's not me."],[657.33,"I'm a Jew from Tarsus, Cilicia."],[659.01,"He says, a citizen of no mean city, the citizen is the important part."],[662.85,"Uh-huh. He drops that card."],[665.64,"Because now he's entitled."],[667.48,"Well, as a Jew who's not a robot citizen, he would have been entitled to nothing."],[672.65,"Zero. Um, as a Roman citizen, now all of a sudden he has rights and everything that have to be respected by these soldiers"],[680.53,"Uh so that drastically changes the whole situation."],[686.69,"So when he had given him permission, Paul stood on the stairs and motioned with his hand to the people."],[692.21,"And when there was a great silence, he spoke to them in the Hebrew language, saying, So notice, the guard says, Okay, go ahead, because again, now that he knows he's a citizen."],[703.89,"Oh, uh, by all means."],[706.53,"Uh, but notice St."],[707.89,"Paul speaks to them in in uh now it says he spoke to them in the Hebrew language, it's more likely that it was actually Aramaic."],[717.17,"Yeah. Um it's what it actually says in the Greek is the language of the Hebrews"],[717.65,"Uhh-hu. Not the yeah, which at this point was was Aramaic."],[728.51,"Um as opposed to Rebever the Guard says, Can you speak Greek?"],[732.85,"Because he spoke to the Roman guard in Greek."],[736.05,"Yeah. Um, but so he's he's speaking because this is a crowd of Jews, he's speaking to them in their own language."],[749.65,"Chapter 22, verse 1."],[751.17,"Brethren and fathers, hear my defense before you now."],[756.45,"And when they heard they heard that he spoke to them in the Hebrew language, they kept all the more silent."],[763.05,"Okay, so they got quieted down, and then he starts speaking it era."],[768.58,"So this is the beginning of maybe this isn't the guy we thought it was."],[772.39,"Maybe the stuff we heard wasn't true."],[775.35,"Then he said, I am indeed a Jew, born in Tarsus of Cilicia, but brought up in this city at the feet of Gamaliel, taught according to the strictness of our father's law, and was zealous toward God as you all are today."],[791.19,"So a couple of things here."],[794.31,"Uh the first thing is we've already seen Gamaliel once in the book of Acts."],[799.75,"Yeah. Well, uh Gamaliel is not, was not only an important name then, Gamaliel's an important name now."],[805.67,"Uh if you get um pretty much any part of the Talmud, which is sort of the big set of of rabbinic traditions that governs rabbinic Judaism today."],[817.15,"If you go to an Orthodox synagogue today."],[820.03,"Um what the Talmud is made up of is just lists of rabbinic commentary."],[827.31,"So you'll have a topic or a law or a passage of scripture, and then it'll say, This rabbi taught X, this rabbi said Y, this rabbi said Z, about this topic."],[840.15,"And Gamaliel's everywhere."],[843.83,"Everywhere. So this isn't only the most prominent rabbi of the first century in Jerusalem."],[849.19,"of This is one the most prominent rabbis in Jewish history."],[858.03,"Even 2,000 years later."],[860.11,"So yes, he's named."],[862.27,"This is more sort of street cred with them."],[864.67,"Yeah, not only do I speak your language, not only am I Jewish."],[868.88,"But look, I studied with Gamaliel."],[873.84,"You know, this is I'm real deal right rabbi here."],[882.08,"The other thing is when it says zealous toward God, um, zeal isn't just an emotion."],[891.02,"Um zealotry is is a tradition within Judaism that's considered to have been founded by Phineas, who a major Jewish hero."],[904.26,"Phineas, in the book of Numbers, which I know isn't one we read a lot for devotional purposes, but Numbers, there's this really horrible episode where right before they're about to go into the land of Canaan, they come to this area called Pa'or, where there are a bunch of Baal worshippers, and uh a bunch of the Israelite men uh notice that some of the local ladies are attractive and decide not only to go and behave in a sexually immoral way with them, but also to go and worship their God with them."],[945.02,"So there's your twofer of idolatry and sexual immorality."],[949.42,"Both at the same time."],[952.06,"And because this is happening and it's so widespread in the Israelite camp, God sends this plague on the camp to make the point this needs to stop."],[963.03,"And despite this plague coming on the camp, the people didn't stop."],[967.21,"Moses and everyone had told them this needs to stop, and they didn't stop."],[970.33,"So finally, Phineas, who is from a priestly family, is one of Aaron's descendants, went and took a spear, went into one of the tents where people were fornicating, and killed a bunch of them."],[982.77,"And when he killed a bunch of them, the plague went away."],[989.41,"And so the point that was sort of being made there in the book of Numbers was that you can't just sort of pay lip service to these guys."],[999.25,"Stop. That's not sort of sufficient."],[1001.99,"It's not endorsing, sort of going and slaughtering people."],[1005.19,"But those were both crimes which under the law had the death penalty, if people didn't repent."],[1011.43,"These people were very unrepentant."],[1014.71,"But so that that created this tradition within Judaism."],[1020.07,"So, for example, we already mentioned Hanukkah tonight."],[1023.19,"When the Maccabean Revolt happened."],[1025.64,"Judas Maccabius and his brothers, they saw what the Greeks had done to the temple, so they rose up in revolt and attacked the Greeks and gained their independence."],[1033.7,"Phineas was sort of their poster person."],[1038.35,"This is evil, this cannot stand."],[1040.83,"We need to go and take action."],[1045.31,"And uh so that that tradition, and that is that tradition is what's identified as zealotry."],[1052.43,"So one of the twelve apostles was St."],[1055.39,"Simon the Zealot."],[1057.21,"And that meant he was there were a number of these zealot groups at this time that were political zealot groups opposed to the Romans, who believed that they should take violent action against the Romans."],[1068.43,"Because of their wickedness and oppression."],[1073.23,"Mostly they took violent actions against Jews who collaborated with the Romans, like tax collectors, and that kind of thing, but um rather than the Romans themselves."],[1081.79,"But so that that whole tradition."],[1083.89,"And that is how we're going to read in his epistles, St."],[1087.65,"Paul looks at what he was doing when he was going around killing Christians like Saint Stephen, going to Damascus to kill Christians when he was when he had his vision of Christ on the road."],[1099.65,"That's how he understood it."],[1101.09,"He was being a zealot"],[1102.69,"He was being a zealot."],[1103.67,"He was doing the right thing like Phineas did."],[1105.95,"Even though he's doing these violent things, what these people were doing was evil, and he needed to purify and stop, put a stop to it."],[1112.87,"So he's even appealing to that now"],[1116.95,"So he's not only name-drop Gabelias, not only speaking to them in Aramaic, not only talking about how he studied the law, but look, I was even zealous, like you are."],[1126.69,"He's attributing them trying to kill him, to this zeal."],[1131.35,"You think I've I'm doing this evil thing."],[1133.99,"You think I brought Greeks into the temple, you think I did these things, and so you want to kill me."],[1139.85,"He's like, I get it."],[1141.55,"I've been there."],[1143.47,"In terms of thinking that way."],[1147.87,"I persecuted the way to the death, binding and delivering into prisons both men and women."],[1154.27,"As also the high priest bears me witness, and all the counsel of the elders, from whom I also received letters to the brethren, and went to Damascus to bring in chains even those who were there in Jerusalem, there to Jerusalem to be punished."],[1169.43,"So he's talking about that former life."],[1171.27,"He's like, Look, I wasn't just part of a mob."],[1175.08,"It was going to kill some."],[1176.68,"I had credentials."],[1178.3,"I had a license to kill."],[1180.03,"From the from the high priest, from the Jewish authorities."],[1182.83,"I was out doing their bidding."],[1184.27,"I was on my way to Damascus, to to go and haul them back in chains to Jerusalem to get taken care of."],[1194.37,"Now it happened as I journeyed and came near Damascus at about noon."],[1199.01,"Suddenly a great light from heaven shone around me, and I fell to the ground and heard a voice saying to me, Saul, Saul, why are you persecuting me?"],[1207.85,"So I answered, Who are you, Lord?"],[1210.17,"And he said to me, I am Jesus of Nazareth, whom you are persecuting."],[1215.37,"So we're reiterating, remember, we read this about twelve chapters ago about this happening the first time."],[1225.61,"And those who were with me indeed saw the light and were afraid, but they did not hear the voice of him who spoke to me."],[1231.95,"That's a little detail that we didn't get the first time."],[1235.15,"That they saw this light, but didn't hear Christ speaking."],[1240.83,"So I said, What shall I do, Lord?"],[1242.75,"And the Lord said to me, Arise and go into Damascus, and there you will be told all things which are appointed for you to do."],[1249.51,"And since I could not see for the glory of the light, being led by the hand of those who are with me, I came into Damascus."],[1257.99,"So he mentions how he was blinded."],[1260.16,"And they had to sort of lead him by the hand there."],[1266.48,"But notice also, remember at the time the first time we heard it, he was told to go to a particular place to get baptized, to find a particular person to get baptized."],[1275.44,"Notice here he says the things which are appointed for you to do."],[1280.2,"It's important that he puts it that way because right now he's defending himself."],[1283.74,"So what's he saying?"],[1284.62,"He's saying all these things I've been doing, when I preach to the Gentiles, when I preach to the Jews, when I preach here, these are all things that the Lord commanded me to do."],[1293.56,"These are things the Lord commanded."],[1294.92,"This isn't just something I, you know, I came up with, you know, my own sect of Judaism to get started."],[1300.7,"Or to build a following for myself."],[1305.1,"Then a certain Ananias, a devout man according to the law, having a good testimony with all the Jews who dwell there."],[1313.34,"Now notice when he talks about Ananias, he doesn't say, I met a Christian there named Adanias."],[1319.74,"In Damascus, he says, you know, this is a pious Jewish man."],[1324.6,"Of good reputation."],[1328.52,"Came to me and he stood and said to me, Brother Saul, receive your sight."],[1332.28,"At that same hour I looked up at him"],[1335.68,"Then he said, The God of our fathers has chosen you that you should know his will and see the just one and hear the voice of his mouth."],[1346.4,"So again, it's God, not just any God, the God of our fathers, the God of Israel."],[1352.49,"The God of the Lord, who picked Saul, now Saint Paul."],[1357.47,"Who picked him for this mission and to do these things."],[1360.59,"And notice know his will and see the just one."],[1364.83,"The just one is one of the titles to refer to the Messiah."],[1370.75,"So he's identifying Jesus here, who appeared to him as the Messiah."],[1373.55,"the Messiah. This is how I know Jesus is"],[1377.03,"He appeared to me in the light of God and told me."],[1397.59,"So that begins with him being baptized and commissioned to this."],[1401.91,"But again, as St."],[1402.79,"Paul is explaining to them, commissioned for this service that he's doing to doing for the God of Israel and for the Messiah."],[1411.07,"Now it happened when I returned to Jerusalem and was praying in the temple, that I was in a trance and saw him saying to me, Make haste and get out of Jerusalem quickly, for they will not receive your testimony concerning me."],[1423.95,"Now, this part we haven't heard about before."],[1427.33,"About why he went to why he went to Antioch in the first place."],[1435.73,"So I said, Lord, they know that in every synagogue I am prisoned and beat those who believe in you."],[1442.45,"So he says, Look, they, you know, they should especially listen to me."],[1448.99,"If they listen to anybody, they should listen to me, because they know I was totally opposed to this."],[1453.39,"I hated this."],[1454.35,"I was out killing people for believing this, and now I'm preaching it."],[1457.73,"That's somebody, and this, you know, this is this is even true in our day."],[1461.01,"We get lots of people who come on TV, the radio, whatever, they say, I'm a former fill in the blank."],[1465.41,"Everybody goes, oh"],[1466.86,"And now I believe the opposite."],[1471.06,"And here's what she said."],[1472.02,"So St. Paul said, hey, they should really listen to me."],[1478.5,"And when the blood of your martyr Stephen was shed, I also was standing by, consenting to his death, and guarding the clothes of those who were killing him."],[1487.24,"We talked about how he served as the coat check guy."],[1491.4,"Now it says you're martyr Stephen."],[1492.84,"The word martyr in Greek means witness."],[1495.3,"Witness. So what's he saying there?"],[1499.38,"How many witnesses did you need, according to the Torah, to establish that something was true?"],[1506.98,"Is it two or three?"],[1508.18,"Two. You had to have two witnesses who had the same testimony"],[1513.82,"Saint Paul saw what?"],[1518.62,"Jesus. What did Saint Stephen see while he was being stoned to death?"],[1526.74,"So he says, when your witness Stephen was killed."],[1531.14,"That's two witnesses."],[1534.92,"That's what St."],[1535.48,"Paul is doing."],[1536.12,"He's saying these there's two witnesses to the fact that Jesus is now enthroned in heaven as the Messiah."],[1544.98,"Me and Saint me and Saint Stephen, who I killed, by the way."],[1548.98,"Back when I believed the other."],[1553.27,"Then he said to me, Depart, for I will send you far from here to the Gentiles."],[1559.59,"Okay. Now we're going to read that they have a real problem with that ending."],[1565.99,"Because what is that ending saying?"],[1569.75,"That ending is saying, just like how Jesus came to his own people and they didn't receive him, they killed him."],[1579.04,"His testimony. God sends Saint Paul to give this testimony."],[1583.3,"They don't believe it."],[1585.38,"So he goes to the Gentiles."],[1587.46,"To some other people."],[1588.74,"That's implying what?"],[1590.02,"That's implying that these Jews who haven't come to believe in Christ have now been rejected by God, aren't the chosen people anymore."],[1597.68,"Unless they come to believe in Jesus as the Messiah."],[1600.72,"They've done it twice."],[1602.0,"Yeah. And they're going to understand that."],[1604.8,"We're about to see that that's what St."],[1606.48,"Paul is saying."],[1608.08,"And they listen to him until this word."],[1611.68,"Until he said that."],[1613.36,"And then they raised their voices and said, Away with such a I like how they translate this in the over the next one."],[1619.36,"Away with such a fellow."],[1623.2,"Doesn't quite capture it."],[1625.84,"Their anger. From the earth, for he is not fit to live."],[1631.76,"You notice the word fellow is in italics."],[1634.0,"Which means they added it."],[1635.36,"Which means that's the word they chose."],[1639.24,"Not such a person, such a blasphemer, no, such a fellow."],[1643.0,"Um. But the idea is more the blasphemer."],[1647.56,"Away with such a blank as this."],[1649.88,"I think all the agents."],[1652.28,"Yeah. Um. Away from the earth."],[1656.3,"Remove him from the earth is what they're saying."],[1659.42,"Because he is not fit to live."],[1661.82,"Then as they cried out and tore off their clothes and threw dust into the air."],[1669.66,"Well, they can't, they want to grab him, but he's got Roman soldiers standing right next to him."],[1674.86,"So if they try and rush at him, and he's told the soldiers he's a Roman citizen."],[1679.23,"So if they try to put their hands on a Roman citizen, the Roman soldiers are just gonna kill them all."],[1682.43,"They're tearing their clothes and kicking up dust"],[1683.43,"So they can't grab him."],[1684.79,"They can't rush him."],[1685.75,"So they're just so angry."],[1690.23,"Aren't these standard uh procedures for registering that emotion?"],[1695.03,"Because don't the high priests do that when well tearing their clothes, yeah, they're throwing dust in the air and stuff is but yeah, they're just sort of uh they're so angry and they can't do anything."],[1704.84,"Because you know, he's standing there with these with these armed uh these armed soldiers."],[1711.56,"It's sort of like uh uh kicking dirt at the umpire."],[1716.36,"You know, you can't touch the umpire or you're gonna get you know fined in a dictionary kick dust at him and the commander ordered him to be brought into the barracks and said that he should be examined under scourging so that he might know why they should why they shouted so against him."],[1740.0,"So yeah, this shows you the Roman mindset."],[1743.57,"So Romans say, okay, bring him inside, because you know they're going crazy."],[1750.05,"Oh, yeah. And so there were there, he could only be scourged a more limited number of times."],[1758.37,"The average. And it's it's for a judicial purpose."],[1764.15,"You can't just trust that someone's gonna tell you the truth because you ask them."],[1768.55,"Oh right. And so you're examined under scourging."],[1770.21,"If they're being beaten, and you say, if you tell me the true truth, I'll stop"],[1775.34,"You can be pretty sure that they're telling you the truth at that point."],[1778.68,"That's the Roman thinking."],[1784.81,"And as they bound him with thongs, Paul said to the centurion who stood by, is it lawful for you to scourge a man who is a Roman and uncondemned?"],[1792.81,"So he says, Don't you technically have to get a judicial decree that I'm to be scourged?"],[1802.17,"So this is the equivalent of this is the first century Roman Empire equivalent of can I see your warrant?"],[1809.29,"That's the So it's not that they weren't allowed to scourge it."],[1812.41,"It's just that these. do you, as a centurion, have the authority to scourge me and question me"],[1819.97,"Now, if they went to the governor, the governor said, Yeah, scourge him and find out what's going on, then they go ahead."],[1826.61,"But what's what's the thing that St."],[1830.37,"Paul's playing here?"],[1831.25,"Well, if St."],[1831.81,"Paul gets brought before the governor, then he'll get to talk to the governor."],[1834.61,"Uh-huh. And be able to speak again to all the people around the governor."],[1842.35,"But the centurion heard that he went and told the commander, saying, Take care what you do what you do, for this man is a Roman."],[1852.69,"So he goes and says, Oh, yeah, we need to be a little careful."],[1856.3,"It's not just that he's a Roman citizen, but it's he's a Roman citizen and he kind of knows what his rights are."],[1864.42,"We're not gonna be able to get away with anything here, so be careful."],[1870.1,"Then the commander came and said to him, Tell me, are you a Roman?"],[1873.46,"He said, Yes."],[1875.14,"The commander answered, with a large sum I obtain this citizenship."],[1880.1,"And Paul said, But I was born a citizen."],[1882.42,"Okay. So the commander doesn't like him."],[1884.66,"Uh-huh. Because he's some Jewish person."],[1887.7,"He says, You're a Roman citizen."],[1889.14,"Well, like he doesn't buy it."],[1891.48,"And uh and that's why St."],[1893.8,"Paul says yes."],[1894.6,"He says, you know, it costs me a lot of money to become a citizen."],[1899.12,"And that was at the end of years and years of military service and everything to earn it."],[1901.16,"He's like, You're just some you know, some Jewish peasant, you know"],[1908.94,"How'd you get Roman citizens?"],[1910.54,"He says, I was born a citizen, which means his father had it."],[1914.06,"And that's that's better."],[1915.66,"That's better. That's generational, so yeah."],[1920.46,"Then immediately those who were about to examine him withdrew from him."],[1923.98,"And the commander was also afraid when he found out that he was a Roman, and because he had bound him."],[1930.4,"So he's like, if he makes a stink, I might even get in trouble for that."],[1937.37,"The next day, because he wanted to know for certain why he was accused by the Jews, he released him from his bonds and commanded the chief priests and all their counsel to appear and brought Paul down and set him before them."],[1949.89,"We'll end up leaving off here."],[1953.41,"But uh so now he has to take a different approach."],[1958.22,"He says, okay, I still need to find out what's going on and why they hate him so much and why all this trouble is being caused."],[1964.14,"I can't beat him."],[1965.66,"You notice he doesn't ask him and trust what he says."],[1971.48,"He's like, oh, I don't buy that."],[1972.6,"It's like what I'll do is I'll get all the people who hate him here."],[1976.62,"I'll put him on a little platform in front of them and ask them to tell me all the reasons they hate him."],[1984.16,"Because again, from a Roman perspective, you can kind of trust hate."],[1986.96,"hate. Somebody's not going to lie about why they someone"],[1991.66,"They might lie about why they love someone."],[1994.63,"They might just be pretending to love them."],[1996.23,"But if somebody really hates somebody, they're going to be honest about why they hate them."],[2001.11,"So that's his that's his thinking here at the end."],[2004.55,"Now remember, we've seen, we're seeing the beginning of St."],[2010.23,"Paul's trials. There's going to be some more."],[2014.33,"But before we end here, I want to remember, remember when he first talked in Ephesus about the fact that he was going to Jerusalem and he was going to be arrested."],[2026.49,"Do you remember what?"],[2027.61,"And this was last time we talked about it."],[2029.53,"Do you remember what he said? his ultimate goal was"],[2033.73,"And sort of his missions."],[2034.93,"He wanted to go to Rome."],[2035.97,"He wanted to get to Caesar."],[2037.65,"Specifically to Caesar."],[2039.33,"He wants to try and convert Caesar."],[2042.05,"So just keep that in the back of your mind as we go through these last few chapters of the book of Acts."],[2047.49,"So it's not about proving that he is honest."],[2051.65,"He's not trying to get off the hook."],[2053.51,"He's trying to reach."],[2054.79,"That's not his goal."],[2055.43,"His goal is to preach the gospel."],[2057.68,"And so we just saw him sort of work his start working his way up toward the governor."],[2062.08,"Uh-huh. And so, you know, if he can't sail to Rome and get an audience with Caesar, well, maybe there's another way."],[2072.38,"I just sort of work my way up there."],[2073.9,"And he's gonna get, as we saw tonight, he got an audience"],[2077.86,"He's gonna keep getting these audiences, these chances to preach, because that's what he's focused on."],[2083.87,"Is preaching the gospel."],[2084.99,"He doesn't care what happens to him."],[2087.55,"As he told us earlier, and he's serious about it."],[2091.31,"So we'll go ahead and end here for tonight."],[2093.95,"We'll pick up in chapter 23 next week."],[2098.35,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2105.71,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2111.07,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":21.36,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 21:26-29 - Purification, then the mob","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Paul takes the four men; next day <b>purified with them</b>, enters temple</li><li class=\"d1\">announces the <b>expiration of the days of purification</b> → offering for each</li><li class=\"d0\">Days of purification before the vow's end: <b>fasting</b> and <b>prayer</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Purified\" = <b>ritual washings</b> before entering the temple, so you were clean</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul <b>still does them</b></li><li class=\"d1\">doesn't say \"old hat, I've been baptized, never need a ritual\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not going along to get back on the good side of the Jews</li><li class=\"d0\">\"If they kill me, okay\" - he does it because it is <b>still valid and important</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Seven days almost ended; the <b>Jews from Asia</b> - the ones following him, causing trouble</li><li class=\"d0\">See him in temple, stir up the whole crowd, lay hands on him</li><li class=\"d0\">Cry: \"Men of Israel, help\" - the man who teaches <b>everywhere against the people, the law, this place</b></li><li class=\"d0\">And \"brought <b>Greeks</b> into the temple\" - defiled the holy place</li><li class=\"d0\">Same stuff they've been badmouthing around town - <b>not true</b></li></ul>"},{"t":129.49,"lv":3,"h":"Greeks in the temple: Hanukkah and Trophimus","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Not that Greeks are horrible - the <b>history</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Hanukkah</b> celebrated every year (Jesus too, in <b>John</b>)</li><li class=\"d1\">= restoration of the temple after the Greeks defiled it</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Antiochus Epiphanes IV</b> sacrificed a <b>pig</b> on the altar</li><li class=\"d1\">Daniel's \"<b>abomination of desolation</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">They appeal to that \"horrible historical atrocity\" in everyone's mind</li><li class=\"d0\">Jews had no authority to execute anyone - but \"get a <b>mob</b> angry enough\" and they'll tear someone apart</li><li class=\"d0\">Had seen <b>Trophimus the Ephesian</b> with him in the city → \"supposed\" Paul brought him into the temple</li><li class=\"d0\">Word \"supposed\": not honestly thought - people saw him around town with Greeks, so \"say he brought them in, they'll believe it\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Fits his reputation: <b>eating with Gentiles</b>, going into their homes</li></ul>"},{"t":249.23,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 21:30-34 - Doors shut; Romans arrest Paul","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">City disturbed, people run together, seize Paul, drag him out of the temple</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Doors shut</b> immediately - temple complex in lockdown</li><li class=\"d0\">Background (early Acts): <b>Jewish temple guards</b></li><li class=\"d1\">deal with Rome: Roman soldiers, being <b>Gentiles</b>, not allowed far into the temple</li><li class=\"d1\">Jewish guards keep order, or Rome sends soldiers in \"we don't care\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Doors shut so Roman authorities see the trouble <b>stays inside</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Romans against a mob: send soldiers, <b>kill everyone</b> until it disperses</li><li class=\"d1\">\"didn't care who it was\" - most effective means</li><li class=\"d0\">Word reaches the <b>garrison commander</b>: all Jerusalem in uproar</li><li class=\"d0\">Takes <b>soldiers and centurions</b>, runs down; mob stops beating Paul - \"nothing to see here\"</li><li class=\"d1\">they knew what would be next</li><li class=\"d0\">Commander has Paul <b>bound with two chains</b>, asks who he is and what he did</li><li class=\"d0\">Roman logic: beaten → <b>he must be the troublemaker</b></li><li class=\"d1\">asks the crowd, not Paul</li><li class=\"d1\">crowd can't get its story straight - \"none of them really know\"; \"he hasn't actually done anything\"</li><li class=\"d1\">different groups yelling different things</li></ul>"},{"t":437.46,"lv":3,"h":"Acts 21:34-36 - Carried up the stairs","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Can't learn the truth for the tumult → into the <b>barracks</b></li><li class=\"d0\">On the stairs <b>carried by soldiers</b> - violence of the mob</li><li class=\"d0\">Mob follows: \"<b>Away with him</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul so beaten he can't make the stairs</li><li class=\"d0\">Roman plan: interrogate, beat, probably kill - an <b>example</b> against more rioting</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul a <b>Roman citizen</b> (earlier in Acts) - \"very few Jews were\"; they'd presume not</li></ul>"},{"t":501.34,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 21:37-38 - Greek? The Egyptian","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">At the barracks door Paul asks: \"May I speak to you\" - before the \"beating, slash torture, slash punishment\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Commander: \"<b>Can you speak Greek?</b> Are you not the <b>Egyptian</b>...\"</li><li class=\"d1\">led <b>4,000 assassins</b> into the wilderness</li><li class=\"d0\">Good thing Paul spoke up - he's being mistaken for someone else</li><li class=\"d0\">Not ethnically Egyptian - Luke's readers all knew who he was</li><li class=\"d0\">One of a sequence of <b>phony messiahs</b>: 1st c. BC → 1st c. AD → <b>Bar Kokhba</b>, early 2nd c.</li><li class=\"d0\">Came from <b>Egypt</b> (huge Jewish community in <b>Alexandria</b>), claimed Messiah, went to the desert with followers as his army</li><li class=\"d1\">not yet caught at this point; later Romans <b>crucified</b> them all</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Jesus prophesied</b> it (Matthew, Luke): \"he's here, he's there\" - don't believe them</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>lightning</b> east to west: \"you'll know when it's me\"</li></ul>"},{"t":644.19,"lv":3,"h":"Acts 21:39-40 - Citizen of Tarsus; Aramaic","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"I am a Jew from <b>Tarsus in Cilicia</b>, a citizen of no mean city\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Citizen</b> is the important part\" - \"he drops that card\"</li><li class=\"d1\">as a Jew not a Roman citizen: entitled to <b>nothing, zero</b></li><li class=\"d1\">as a Roman: <b>rights</b> soldiers must respect → \"drastically changes the whole situation\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Asks permission to speak to the people</li><li class=\"d0\">Commander says go ahead - \"by all means\", now that he's a citizen</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul on the <b>stairs</b>, motions with his hand; <b>great silence</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Hebrew language\" = literally \"language of the Hebrews\" → at this point <b>Aramaic</b>, not Hebrew</li><li class=\"d0\">Spoke <b>Greek</b> to the Roman; to this crowd of Jews, <b>their own language</b></li></ul>"},{"t":749.65,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 22:1-3 - Defense: Tarsus and Gamaliel","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Brethren and fathers</b>, hear my defense\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Hearing Aramaic → they kept <b>all the more silent</b></li><li class=\"d1\">start of \"maybe this isn't the guy we thought; maybe what we heard wasn't true\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"A Jew, born in <b>Tarsus</b>, brought up in this city at the feet of <b>Gamaliel</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">taught by the strictness of the fathers' law; <b>zealous toward God</b> as you are today</li><li class=\"d0\">Seen once already in Acts</li><li class=\"d0\">A name still important today: the <b>Talmud</b> = lists of <b>rabbinic commentary</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"This rabbi taught X, that rabbi Y\" - \"<b>Gamaliel's everywhere</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not just the top rabbi of 1st-c. Jerusalem - one of the most prominent in <b>Jewish history</b>, 2,000 years on</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Street cred\": speak your language, Jewish, studied with Gamaliel - \"real deal rabbi\"</li></ul>"},{"t":882.08,"lv":3,"h":"Zeal and Phinehas","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Zeal</b> isn't just an emotion - <b>zealotry</b> a tradition founded by <b>Phinehas</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Numbers</b> (Peor), before entering <b>Canaan</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Israelite men with local women: sexual immorality + worshiping their god - \"a twofer\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>plague</b> on the camp; Moses and others told them to stop; they didn't</li><li class=\"d1\">Phinehas, of <b>Aaron's</b> priestly line, took a <b>spear</b> into a tent, killed them → plague stopped</li><li class=\"d0\">Point: can't just <b>pay lip service</b>; both crimes carried the <b>death penalty</b> if unrepentant</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not endorsing going and slaughtering people\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1020.07,"lv":3,"h":"The zealot tradition and Paul's own zeal","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Hanukkah</b> tonight: <b>Maccabean Revolt</b> - <b>Judas Maccabeus</b> and brothers rose against the Greeks</li><li class=\"d1\">Phinehas their \"poster person\": \"this is evil, cannot stand, take action\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Simon the Zealot</b>, one of the Twelve</li><li class=\"d1\">political zealot groups vs <b>Rome</b>, violent action</li><li class=\"d1\">mostly against <b>collaborators</b> (tax collectors), not Romans</li><li class=\"d0\">Epistles: Paul sees his persecution (<b>Stephen</b>, going to <b>Damascus</b>) as being a <b>zealot</b>, \"doing the right thing like Phinehas\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Now appeals to it:</li><li class=\"d1\">name-drops Gamaliel, speaks Aramaic, studied the law, \"I was even <b>zealous like you</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">attributes their trying to kill him to <b>zeal</b>: \"I get it, I've been there\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1147.87,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 22:4-11 - Persecutor; Damascus road retold","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"I persecuted <b>the Way</b> to the death\", <b>men and women</b>, into prison</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>High priest</b> and whole council of elders bear witness</li><li class=\"d0\">Had <b>letters</b> to the brethren at Damascus, to bring them in chains to Jerusalem</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Not just part of a mob\" - \"<b>a license to kill</b>\" from the Jewish authorities, doing their bidding</li><li class=\"d0\">About <b>noon</b>, great light from heaven, falls to the ground</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Saul, Saul</b>, why are you persecuting me?\" - \"I am <b>Jesus of Nazareth</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Read the first telling ~twelve chapters ago</li><li class=\"d0\">New detail: companions saw the light and were afraid but <b>did not hear the voice</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Blinded by the glory; <b>led by the hand</b> into Damascus</li><li class=\"d0\">First telling: sent to a particular place and person for <b>baptism</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Here: \"things which are <b>appointed for you to do</b>\" - chosen because he's defending himself</li><li class=\"d1\">preaching to Gentiles, to Jews, here = <b>commanded by the Lord</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"not my own sect of Judaism\" or a following for myself</li></ul>"},{"t":1305.1,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 22:12-16 - Ananias","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"A devout man according to the <b>law</b>, good testimony with all the Jews\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul doesn't say \"a Christian named Ananias\" - a <b>pious Jewish man</b> of good reputation</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Brother Saul, receive your sight\" - at that hour he looked up</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>The God of our fathers</b> has chosen you\" - the God of Israel</li><li class=\"d1\">to <b>know his will</b>, see <b>the Just One</b>, hear the voice of his mouth</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Just One\" = a <b>title of the Messiah</b> → Jesus appeared to him as Messiah</li><li class=\"d0\">Begins with baptism and <b>commissioning</b> - service for the God of Israel and the Messiah</li></ul>"},{"t":1411.07,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 22:17-20 - Temple vision; two witnesses","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Back in Jerusalem, <b>praying in the temple</b>, in a trance: \"Make haste, get out of Jerusalem - they won't receive your testimony\"</li><li class=\"d1\">new: why he went to <b>Antioch</b> in the first place</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul: \"they know I imprisoned and beat believers in every synagogue\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"if they listen to anybody, they should listen to me\" - hated this, was killing for it</li><li class=\"d0\">Like \"I'm a former so-and-so\" speakers on TV today: everyone goes \"oh\" - \"now I believe the opposite\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"When the blood of your martyr <b>Stephen</b> was shed I was standing by, consenting, guarding the clothes\" - the \"coat check guy\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Martyr</b> = <b>witness</b> in Greek</li><li class=\"d0\">Torah: <b>two witnesses</b> with the same testimony to establish a matter</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul saw <b>Jesus</b>; Stephen saw him while being stoned</li><li class=\"d1\">two witnesses that Jesus is <b>enthroned in heaven as Messiah</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"me and Stephen, whom I killed, back when I believed the other\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1553.27,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 22:21-23 - \"I will send you to the Gentiles\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Depart, I will send you far from here to the <b>Gentiles</b>\" - they have a real problem with that ending</li><li class=\"d0\">Same pattern as Jesus: came to his own, <b>not received, killed</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God sends Paul with testimony; not believed → <b>to the Gentiles</b></li><li class=\"d1\">implies Jews who haven't believed are <b>rejected by God</b>, no longer chosen unless they believe in Jesus as Messiah - \"done it twice\"</li><li class=\"d0\">They listened <b>until this word</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Away with such a fellow from the earth, he is not fit to live\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"fellow\" in <b>italics</b> = translators added it; not the sense</li><li class=\"d0\">Idea: \"away with such a <b>blasphemer</b>\" / \"such a blank as this\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Remove him from the earth</b></li><li class=\"d0\">They want to grab him but <b>Roman soldiers</b> stand beside him</li><li class=\"d1\">touching a Roman citizen → soldiers \"kill them all\"</li><li class=\"d0\">So: tearing clothes, <b>throwing dust</b> - standard expressions of emotion (high priests tear clothes)</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: standard way to register emotion? A: yes - so angry, can't act</li><li class=\"d1\">\"kicking dirt at the umpire\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1716.36,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 22:24-26 - Examined under scourging","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Commander orders him into the barracks, <b>examined under scourging</b> - to learn why they shouted</li><li class=\"d0\">The Roman mindset: for a <b>judicial purpose</b></li><li class=\"d1\">can't trust someone to tell the truth because you ask</li><li class=\"d1\">beaten, \"tell me the truth and I'll stop\" → \"you can be pretty sure\" it's true</li><li class=\"d0\">Limited number of scourgings</li><li class=\"d0\">Bound with thongs; Paul to the <b>centurion</b>: lawful to scourge a man who is <b>Roman and uncondemned</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\">= \"can I see your <b>warrant</b>?\" - need a judicial decree</li><li class=\"d1\">not that they couldn't scourge - does a centurion have the authority?</li><li class=\"d0\">If the <b>governor</b> said yes, they'd proceed</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul's play: before the governor, he gets to <b>speak again</b> to the people around him</li><li class=\"d0\">Centurion tells the commander: \"Take care what you do, this man is a Roman\"</li><li class=\"d1\">a citizen who <b>knows his rights</b> - \"not gonna get away with anything\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1870.1,"lv":3,"h":"Acts 22:27-29 - \"I was born a citizen\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Commander: \"Are you a Roman?\" - \"Yes\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"With a large sum I obtained this citizenship\" - doesn't buy it: \"some Jewish peasant\"</li><li class=\"d1\">cost money, after years of <b>military service</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul: \"But I was <b>born</b> a citizen\" → his father had it - \"<b>generational</b>\", better</li><li class=\"d0\">Examiners withdraw at once; commander <b>afraid</b> - he had bound him</li><li class=\"d1\">\"if he makes a stink, I might even get in trouble\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1937.37,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 22:30 - Council convened; Paul's aim: Caesar","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Next day, wanting the truth, commander <b>releases his bonds</b>, commands the <b>chief priests and council</b> to appear; Paul set before them</li><li class=\"d0\">\"We'll end up leaving off here\" - a different approach</li><li class=\"d1\">can't beat him; won't trust what he says</li><li class=\"d1\">plan: all who hate him in one place, on a platform: \"tell me why you hate him\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Roman view: \"you can kind of trust <b>hate</b>\" - people may lie about why they love, not why they hate</li><li class=\"d0\">Beginning of <b>Paul's trials</b>; more to come</li><li class=\"d0\">At Ephesus his ultimate goal: <b>Rome</b>, <b>Caesar</b> - \"wants to try and convert Caesar\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Keep it in mind through the last chapters of Acts</li><li class=\"d1\">not proving he's honest or getting off the hook</li><li class=\"d1\">goal = <b>preach the gospel</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Working up toward the governor; if he can't sail to Rome, \"work my way up there\"</li><li class=\"d1\">keeps getting <b>audiences</b>, chances to preach</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Doesn't care what happens to him\" - and serious about it</li></ul>"}],"next":"Next week: <b>Acts 23</b>"});
